BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Buzz Kull "Deep Hate" Live in Canberra
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20260627T190000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20260627T220000
DTSTAMP:20260620T134450
UID:ganggang-10002063-1782586800-1782597600@ganggangcafe.com.au
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://ganggangcafe.com.au/wp-content/uploads/20
 26/06/Screenshot-2026-06-17-at-2.35.41-pm.png
CREATED:20260617T043619Z
DESCRIPTION:Fresh off the release of his new EP Deep Hate via Heartworm 
 Press\, Buzz Kull heads to Canberra for an intimate headline show at The A
 byss (The Basement). \n\n\n\nIn recent years\, the Sydney dark electronic 
 mainstay has toured Australia with Molchat Doma and Boy Harsher\, the Unit
 ed States with Cold Cave\, and Europe with Kontravoid\, cementing his repu
 tation as one of the underground’s most commanding live acts. \n\n\n\nDe
 ep Hate sees Marc Dwyer at his most focused and ferocious\, delivering fo
 ur relentless industrial pop cuts steeped in nocturnal atmosphere. \n\n\n\
 nAt Nighthawks\, experience Deep Hate up close in one of Canberra’s mo
 st immersive late-night rooms
LAST-MODIFIED:20260617T043620Z
LOCATION:Gang Gang Cafe\, Shop 4/2 Frencham Pl\, Downer ACT 2602
ORGANIZER:Gang Gang Cafe
URL:https://ganggangcafe.com.au/event/buzz-kull-deep-hate-live-in-canberra
 /
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Gang Gang Comedy - Suma Iyer
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20260702T193000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20260702T213000
DTSTAMP:20260620T134450
UID:ganggang-10002062-1783020600-1783027800@ganggangcafe.com.au
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://ganggangcafe.com.au/wp-content/uploads/20
 26/06/Screenshot-2026-06-16-at-11.19.59-am.png
CREATED:20260616T012153Z
DESCRIPTION:Gang Gang Comedy brings you the best comedians from around the
  country. This July we have rising comedy star Suma Iyer. Local supports w
 ill be the very funny Dylan Holmes\, newcomer Cruze Batcheldor\, and every
 one’s favourite Chris Ryan. Your MC for the evening is the one and only 
 Maddy Weeks.  \n\n\n\nFresh off a successful comedy festival season\, tou
 ring Adelaide and Sydney\, Suma Iyer is back in town ready to make you lau
 gh. Winner of the Raw Comedy ACT state final for 2024\, Suma’s cleverly 
 constructed and relatable observations and stories will keep you laughing 
 long after the show has ended. \n\n\n\n“This one’s star is going to ri
 se” – The List UK \n\n\n\nDoors at 7pm for a 7:30pm show start. \n\n\n
 \nTix $22 online Humanitix\, $25 at the door.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260616T012154Z
LOCATION:Gang Gang Cafe\, Shop 4/2 Frencham Pl\, Downer ACT 2602
ORGANIZER:Gang Gang Cafe
URL:https://ganggangcafe.com.au/event/gang-gang-comedy-suma-iyer/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Cut Worms (USA) with special guest John Andrews (USA)
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20260709T190000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20260709T220000
DTSTAMP:20260620T134450
UID:ganggang-10001243-1783623600-1783634400@ganggangcafe.com.au
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://ganggangcafe.com.au/wp-content/uploads/20
 26/03/Screenshot-2026-03-17-at-11.30.21-am.png
CREATED:20260317T003144Z
DESCRIPTION:Transmitter is Max Clarke’s fourth full length record as C
 ut Worms\, due out March 13th via JagJaguwar. Produced by Jeff Tweedy at W
 ilco’s Loft studio\, Transmitter marks a deepening of Clarke’s abili
 ties and the convergence of two artists whose work searches for grace amid
  dislocation. Together\, they conjure the ecstatic spirits of power pop an
 d alt rock\, expanding Cut Worms’ vintage palette while reaffirming his 
 gift for timeless songwriting. \n\n\n\nWhile Clarke’s voice and writing 
 formed the framework\, Tweedy’s guitar and bass lines sketched the rooms
  the songs inhabit. Tweedy’s presence as a producer revealed itself not 
 in heavy-handed choices but in how he coloured spaces and continually offe
 red new textures. Between them\, their like-minded sensibilities bridged a
  generational gap to create something more nuanced than either might have 
 made alone. \n\n\n\nNow several albums into his career\, Clarke stands ful
 ly in command of his craft\, resonating at his own frequency. What began a
 s a passion for bygone pop has matured into a study of endurance itself\, 
 confirming him as a singer-songwriter of lasting depth. Transmitter finds 
 Clarke in full stride\, writing with the conviction of someone who’s mad
 e peace with uncertainty. These songs reckon with the cost of comfort and 
 return to the idea that beauty\, connection\, and love are not luxuries bu
 t necessities for survival. \n\n\n\nJohn Andrews has spent the past few ye
 ars tucked away in Red Hook\, Brooklyn – a neighborhood that sits just b
 eyond the natural drift of the city. Once shaped by maritime industry and 
 later a haven for artists in search of vast warehouse space\, its history 
 and isolation give it a quiet magnetism. Streetsweeper\, the fifth album
  by John Andrews & The Yawns\, reflects that vantage point-tranquil\, self
 -contained\, and curious about the movements most people overlook. \n\n\n\
 n\n\n\n\nGang Gang is committed to an inclusive and safe experience for al
 l. Gang Gang Cafe is wheelchair accessible with accessible restrooms. We h
 ave zero tolerance for harassment and have support measures in place to en
 sure everyone’s safety. For specific accessibility needs or assistance\,
  please contact us in advance. We aim to make our events enjoyable for eve
 ryone. \n\n\n\nGang Gang Cafe acknowledges the Ngunnawal and Ngambri peopl
 e\, the Traditional Custodians of the land where our events take place. We
  pay our respects to their Elders past\, present\, and emerging\, and reco
 gnise their enduring connection to this land\, waters\, and culture. We ar
 e grateful to celebrate music and dance on Ngunnawal Country.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260414T065350Z
LOCATION:Gang Gang Cafe\, Shop 4/2 Frencham Pl\, Downer ACT 2602
ORGANIZER:Gang Gang Cafe
URL:https://ganggangcafe.com.au/event/cut-worms-usa-with-special-guest-joh
 n-andrews-usa/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Miss Kaninna
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20260711T190000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20260711T220000
DTSTAMP:20260620T134450
UID:ganggang-10002064-1783796400-1783807200@ganggangcafe.com.au
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://ganggangcafe.com.au/wp-content/uploads/20
 26/06/Screenshot-2026-06-18-at-8.58.56-am.png
CREATED:20260617T230355Z
DESCRIPTION:Sometimes we have people play at the cafe who have such an imp
 act that it’s a little bittersweet\, they’re so good that they’re go
 ing to be too big for us to ever get them back. Miss Kaninna was one of th
 ose sets at our festival Sundowner. She has been blowing up ever since (su
 pported Kneecap in the UK/Europe) and we are so stoked she is keen to come
  back.Miss Kaninna \n\n\n\nMiss Kaninna is a First Nations artist whose mu
 sic\, voice\, and presence have made her one of \n\n\n\nthe most compellin
 g figures in so-called Australian music today. Hailing from Bruny Island\,
  \n\n\n\nTasmania\, she is of Yorta Yorta\, Dja Dja Wurrung\, Kalkadoon\, 
 and Yirendali heritage. She made \n\n\n\nhistory in 2024 with her debut si
 ngle\, Blak Britney\, earning three ARIA nominations\, including \n\n\n\nB
 est Independent Release\, becoming the first independent Aboriginal woman 
 nominated for an \n\n\n\nARIA for a debut single. The track reached #1 on 
 triple j\, featured in Netflix’s Heartbreak High \n\n\n\nand was named b
 y Rolling Stone as one of the Best Australian & NZ Songs of the 21st Centu
 ry\, \n\n\n\nmarking a critical and cultural breakthrough. \n\n\n\nHer deb
 ut EP\, KANINNA\, followed to critical acclaim\, winning Best Independent 
 Hip-Hop \n\n\n\nEP/Album and Breakthrough Independent Artist of the Year a
 t the 2025 Australian Independent \n\n\n\nMusic (AIR) Awards\, and receivi
 ng an ARIA nomination for Best Hip-Hop Release. \n\n\n\nIn late 2025\, Mis
 s Kaninna took her music overseas\, joining Irish rappers Kneecap\, for an
  \n\n\n\n18-date sold out tour across the UK and Europe. From Amsterdam to
  Glasgow\, her ferocious \n\n\n\ncharisma\, rage\, and resistance made eve
 ry performance an uncompromising statement of \n\n\n\nidentity and truth. 
 \n\n\n\nAt home\, she has supported Amyl and the Sniffers\, Hiatus Kaiyote
  and M.I.A\, whilst sharing \n\n\n\nstages with Stormzy\, Steve Lacy\, and
  Raye on the 2024 Laneway Festival tour. She was named \n\n\n\ntriple j Un
 earthed Artist of the Year\, received SXSW Sydney’s inaugural Justin Cos
 by Award for \n\n\n\nBest New Talent\, and was included in NME’s 2025 Es
 sential 100 Emerging Artists. In 2026\, \n\n\n\nAmazon named her one of th
 eir Global Artists to Watch. \n\n\n\nMiss Kaninna’s reputation as a live
  performer rests on her ability to hold space\, rousing rage \n\n\n\nand j
 oy in equal measure. Floating effortlessly between Hip-Hop\, R&B\, rock an
 d pop\, her \n\n\n\ngenre-defying approach to performance provides a staun
 ch foundation for a new artist with an \n\n\n\nurgency for change. With ac
 tivism a crucial thread in her lineage and her art\, contributing her \n\n
 \n\nplatform and support to marginalised communities form a vital part of 
 her practise. In 2025 she \n\n\n\nspearheaded the creation of Sovereign Da
 y Out – a festival to uplift First Nations people \n\n\n\nfollowing a wh
 ite supremacist attack on sacred land – and continues ongoing work with 
 \n\n\n\ninitiatives supporting Indigenous\, immigrant\, LGBTQI+ and women
 ’s rights. \n\n\n\nWith each milestone and movement\, Miss Kaninna conti
 nues to solidify her place as an artist \n\n\n\nwhose voice and presence c
 ommand attention. She is a cultural leader\, a creative force\, and a \n\n
 \n\nperformer whose influence extends far beyond the stage.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260617T230356Z
LOCATION:Gang Gang Cafe\, Shop 4/2 Frencham Pl\, Downer ACT 2602
ORGANIZER:Gang Gang Cafe
URL:https://ganggangcafe.com.au/event/miss-kaninna/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Leah Senior
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20260809T180000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20260809T220000
DTSTAMP:20260620T134450
UID:ganggang-10002052-1786298400-1786312800@ganggangcafe.com.au
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://ganggangcafe.com.au/wp-content/uploads/20
 26/05/Screenshot-2026-05-19-at-10.19.38-am.png
CREATED:20260519T002012Z
DESCRIPTION:Australian folk diviner Leah Senior makes her way to Canberr
 a with her band in June to launch her fifth studio album Pt. Roadknight.P
 t. Roadknight explores Leah’s introspective\, nature-loving side while 
 honing the singular baroque psych folk that has captivated listeners aroun
 d the world. While the style and instrumentation of ‘70s Brit folk are t
 ouchstones on Senior’s forthcoming album\, her disarming lyrics are fres
 h and wholehearted\, wrestling with modern concerns of gentrification and 
 isolation while finding solace in the quiet beauty of the Victoria surf co
 ast town where she lives. \n\n\n\nA shining star of the Australian folk sc
 ene for the past decade\, Leah Senior’s past four records have received 
 critical acclaim from global media and radio stations\, with Leah touring 
 extensively\, sharing stages with the likes of Wilco\, Iron & Wine\, Simon
  Joyner\, Jessica Pratt\, and King Gizzard and The Lizard Wizard.  \n\n\n
 \nThe new album Pt. Roadknight marks an exciting new chapter in Leah Sen
 ior’s musical journey\, affirming her as one of Australia’s most authe
 ntic folk storytellers.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260519T002015Z
LOCATION:Gang Gang Cafe\, Shop 4/2 Frencham Pl\, Downer ACT 2602
ORGANIZER:Gang Gang Cafe
URL:https://ganggangcafe.com.au/event/leah-senior/
END:VEVENT
