BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Select Music presents Felipe Baldomir 'Sunset Highway' Tour
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20260827T190000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20260827T223000
DTSTAMP:20260620T134450
UID:ganggang-10002050-1787857200-1787869800@ganggangcafe.com.au
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://ganggangcafe.com.au/wp-content/uploads/20
 26/05/Screenshot-2026-05-12-at-10.00.06-am.png
CREATED:20260512T000241Z
DESCRIPTION:Words from Felipe: \n\n\n\n“Australia! I am so excited to be
  heading on tour this winter (Jul-Sep) to celebrate the first four singles
  of my upcoming fourth album! \n\n\n\nThe new music is already starting to
  drop\, and I cannot wait to play it live alongside the classic favourites
 ! The Sunset Highway Australian Tour 2026 is now on sale – let’s go!!
 ” \n\n\n\nFelipe Baldomir is a coastal indie-folk singer-songwriter and 
 multi-instrumentalist from Uruguay\, now based in Byron Bay\, Australia. \
 n\n\n\nKnown for his feel-good sound & dynamic live-looping performances\,
  he blends folk with groovy guitar riffs\, drums\, synths\, and saxophone 
 to deliver a full-band energy show as a solo artist. Since relocating to A
 ustralia in 2018\, Felipe has built a global audience through relentless t
 ouring – evolving from busking and van life into sold-out headline shows
  and festival appearances across Europe\, the UK\, Australia\, North Ameri
 ca\, and beyond. \n\n\n\nFelipe has just announced that his fourth studio 
 album will arrive this November 2026.Featuring a wave of fresh coastal sou
 nds inspired by outdoor living in Australia and a deep connection to surfi
 ng\, his songwriting reflects a sense of flow\, openness\, and adventure. 
 Felipe writes with the stage in mind\, making the music all about bringing
  people together &creating an uplifting experience. With a strong internat
 ional touring presence and a reputation for engaging live shows\, Felipe i
 s steadily carving out his place within the global indie scene. \n\n\n\nTh
 e Sunset Highway Australian Tour 2026 is now live & on sale.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260512T000244Z
LOCATION:Gang Gang Cafe\, Shop 4/2 Frencham Pl\, Downer ACT 2602
ORGANIZER:Gang Gang Cafe
URL:https://ganggangcafe.com.au/event/select-music-presents-felipe-baldomi
 r-sunset-highway-tour/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Shock Corridor - Album Tour with Dumbhead
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20260905T180000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20260905T220000
DTSTAMP:20260620T134450
UID:ganggang-10002060-1788631200-1788645600@ganggangcafe.com.au
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://ganggangcafe.com.au/wp-content/uploads/20
 26/06/Screenshot-2026-06-16-at-11.12.58-am.png
CREATED:20260616T011322Z
DESCRIPTION:Naarm/Melbourne sextet Shock Corridor announce a national tour
  in support of their self-titled debut album\, due August 12. The run open
 s August 28 at Melbourne’s Thornbury Theatre and winds through Sydney’
 s Oxford Art Factory\, Canberra\, Adelaide\, Wonder Mountain Festival in B
 eechworth\, Castlemaine and Brisbane through late September with a one-off
  Sydney show at Phoenix Central Park on June 24 to preview the record in f
 ull. \n\n\n\nThe album was tracked over seven days at Soundpark Studios wi
 th producer Dan Luscombe\, a name synonymous with the last decade of Austr
 alian guitar music for his work with the Drones\, Amyl and the Sniffers\, 
 Courtney Barnett and Floodlights\, and mixed by Aaron Cupples (Spiritualiz
 ed\, Tropical Fuck Storm\, Kirin J Callinan). \n\n\n\nFormed in 2019 by si
 x friends with backgrounds in classical strings\, jazz\, hip-hop and DIY e
 lectronics\, the band\, George (vocals\, guitar)\, Saskia (violin\, vocals
 )\, Joe (synth\, drum machine\, trumpet)\, Henry (bass\, trumpet)\, Ari (g
 uitar) and Paddy (drums)\, refined a startlingly singular palette through 
 long lockdown rehearsals before emerging onto the Naarm circuit in 2023. T
 heir music borrows the spectral patience of the Dirty Three\, the trip-hop
  weight of Massive Attack and the pent-up theatricality that Australian po
 st-punk seems to manufacture in unusual quantities. Songs build slowly\; e
 ruptions\, when they come\, feel earned. \n\n\n\nEarlier singles “Buster
 ” and “Sheet Metal” pulled support from BBC 6 Music\, METAL\, ASBO a
 nd the Line of Best Fit\, while FBi Radio recently named the group their I
 ndependent Artist of the Week. In December the band sold out The Night Cat
  (650 capacity) at home and have shared stages with Bleak Squad at the Mel
 bourne Recital Centre and Floodlights on the road. \n\n\n\n“We kept the 
 record self-titled because it felt like the widest possible foundation of 
 what Shock Corridor is. A lot of it was written while the world felt incre
 asingly unstable — there was this constant feeling of helplessness\, but
  also a desire to stay connected to the people around you. The album lives
  in that tension.”
LAST-MODIFIED:20260616T011323Z
LOCATION:Gang Gang Cafe\, Shop 4/2 Frencham Pl\, Downer ACT 2602
ORGANIZER:Gang Gang Cafe
URL:https://ganggangcafe.com.au/event/shock-corridor-album-tour-with-dumbh
 ead/
END:VEVENT
